<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sous</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Souss</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sous is a region of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, the fertile valley of the Sous river between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlas-mountains">High Atlas</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anti-atlas">Anti-Atlas</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agadir">Agadir</a> and Taroudant as its main towns. Long a land of Amazigh tribes and religious lodges, it was the base from which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saadi-dynasty">Saadi dynasty</a> rose in the early 16th century, and later of the marabout state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tazeroualt">Tazeroualt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sous.jpg" alt="Sous" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MPF · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Argania_spinosa_habitat2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
